input:
You are tasked with writing a program that reads a well-formed XML file and converts it into a JSON file. The XML file may contain elements, attributes, and nested structures. Your program should parse the XML file and generate a JSON representation that accurately reflects the structure and data of the XML file. The JSON output should be formatted with an indentation of 4 spaces.

**Input:**
- A well-formed XML file named `input.xml`.

**Output:**
- A JSON file named `output.json` that represents the XML file's structure and data.

**Sample Input (input.xml):**
```xml
<library>
    <book id="1">
        <title>Python Programming</title>
        <author>John Doe</author>
        <year>2021</year>
    </book>
    <book id="2">
        <title>Data Structures</title>
        <author>Jane Smith</author>
        <year>2019</year>
    </book>
</library>
```

**Sample Output (output.json):**
```json
{
    "library": {
        "book": [
            {
                "attributes": {
                    "id": "1"
                },
                "title": {
                    "text": "Python Programming"
                },
                "author": {
                    "text": "John Doe"
                },
                "year": {
                    "text": "2021"
                }
            },
            {
                "attributes": {
                    "id": "2"
                },
                "title": {
                    "text": "Data Structures"
                },
                "author": {
                    "text": "Jane Smith"
                },
                "year": {
                    "text": "2019"
                }
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

